 ### Cost and caps
 
-Cost per escalated task, counted rather than measured: escalation 1 adds 1 adviser spawn (2 when the executor is known to be on the top rung), escalation 2 adds 2, each of those two escalations adds at most 1 critique spawn (only when no answer passed), escalation 3 adds none, and every attempt gets one QA review as today. Worst case: 5 reviews instead of 2, and at most 6 adviser spawns (2 at escalation 1, 2 at escalation 2, plus 2 critiques).
+Cost per escalated task, counted rather than measured: escalation 1 adds 1 adviser spawn (2 when the executor is known to be on the top rung), escalation 2 adds 2, each of those two escalations adds at most 1 critique spawn (only when no answer passed), escalation 3 adds none, and every attempt gets one QA review as today. Worst case: 9 reviews instead of 2 (5 ladder reviews, at most 2 repair re-reviews and at most 2 inline-review re-runs, one each for A1 and A2, `refs/qa.md`), and at most 6 adviser spawns (2 at escalation 1, 2 at escalation 2, plus 2 critiques).
+
+Each review may also spawn one reviewer respawn (up to 18 reviewer spawns per task). Each crash during a review adds one Row V re-review (Resume in `refs/ledger.md`). A resume into an escalation whose advice was not recorded spawns that escalation's advisers again (counted per pass). Each resume after a halt adds one operator review. Per run: at most `RETRY_BUDGET` tasks enter the ladder (When the ladder runs, check 4).
+
+Repairs: at most 1 per attempt, except the second A2 repair (Repair round), and at most 2 per task, counted as `repair-<k>-<j>.md` files, so a resume gives the same answer. A repair writes no `step=open` record, so it does not spend a `RETRY_BUDGET` slot. Reverts: at most 3, and only on the adviser route; a repair never reverts.
 
-Each review may also spawn one reviewer respawn (up to 10 reviewer spawns per task). A resume into an escalation whose advice was not recorded spawns that escalation's advisers again (counted per pass). Each resume after a halt adds one operator review. Per run: at most `RETRY_BUDGET` tasks enter the ladder (When the ladder runs, check 4).
+No token cap. Token use is not written to the ledger or any retry file, because resume dispatches from the ledger alone and a token gate could not be recomputed on resume; the attempt and spawn caps above already bound the worst case.
 
